From 1767480991e6167a49709e7ae58fe5fe240ba14e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:45:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: record block processing and assembly timings as
 numeric fields

Convert 13 BENCH debug producers. Preserve exact two/three-decimal readable timing text, original clock reads and calculations, per-input zero guards, accumulated seconds and mean milliseconds per block. Timing values remain numeric rather than formatted message fragments; all computation remains behind existing category/level gates.

Scripted diff commands:
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/block-processing-timing-diagnostics.json --report /private/tmp/logging-core-timing-report.json --apply
git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style "{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}" HEAD -- src/validation.cpp src/node/miner.cpp
python3 test/lint/lint-log-events.py src/validation.cpp src/node/miner.cpp
git diff --check

Source-only: NOT_COMPILED / NOT_RUN. No benchmark measurements or performance claim; actual renderer/runtime checks deferred to the combined validation gate.
